Package: stareal
Title: Spatial-Temporal Areal Estimation from Survey Data
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Robert", "Verity", , "r.verity@imperial.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bayesian space-time models for binomial survey data on a set of
    areal units (e.g. administrative units) and a regular time grid. The latent
    field is separable: a conditional autoregressive prior in space (Leroux,
    BYM2 or proper CAR) and a first-order autoregressive prior in time, plus
    fixed effects and a cell-level nugget. Main effects in space and in time
    (autoregressive, or first- or second-order random walks) can be added,
    and the space-time interaction chosen among Knorr-Held's four types.
    Because the prior is Gaussian, the
    unobserved area-time cells are integrated out exactly, so the model is
    fitted on the observed cells only. The full area-by-time table is then
    reconstructed by conditional simulation, one surface per posterior draw,
    and aggregated draw by draw to coarser groupings. Models are compared by
    cross-validation, or from one fit by leave-one-out with each cell's own
    latent value integrated out.
